{"abstract":"The notion of software ecosystems has been popular both in research and industry for more than a decade, but how software ecosystems are created still remains unclear. This becomes more of a challenge if one examines the \"creation'' of ecosystems that have high probability in surviving in the future, i.e. with respect to ecosystem health. In this paper, we focus on the creation of software ecosystems and propose a process for designing, developing, and establishing software ecosystems based on three basic steps and a set of activities for each step. We note that software ecosystem research identifies that ecosystems typically emerge from either a company deciding to allow development on their product platform or from a successful open source project. In our study we add to this knowledge by demonstrating, through two case studies, that ecosystems can emerge from more than a technological infrastructure (platform). We identify that ecosystems can emerge out of two more distinct types of environments and thus the design should be based on the characteristics of this categorization. Moreover, we follow the approach that design, development, and establishment are not three distinct phases but rather aspects of a single re-iterating phase and thus propose the view of design, development, and establishment as a continous process, running in parallel with and interrelated to the monitoring of the ecosystem evolution.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Manikas, Konstantinos","Hämäläinen, Mervi","Tyrväinen, Pasi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-492248"],"event":{"end":"2016-12-10","place":"Dublin, ie","start":"2016-12-10","title":"8th International Workshop on Software Ecosystems","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Jyväskylä"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DHYI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DHYI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designing developing and implementing software ecosystems towards a step wise guide","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/179276181/Manikas_2017_Designing_developing_and_implementing.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-492248","ids":["ku-a568906d-4d32-44dd-9ecc-671a14fa6baf"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-D7A7BE275B5F69A7FFAF079BBF33D41C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/179276181/Manikas_2017_Designing_developing_and_implementing.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://ceur-ws.org/Vol-1808/IWSECO16-paper5-Manikas-p70-79.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The HCC Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dhi danish hydraulic institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DHYI","l3nn":"DHI Danish Hydraulic Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DHI Danish Hydraulic Institute","namevar":["DHI GRAS A/S (Biz)"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DHYI","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fi","key":"university of jyväskylä","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Jyväskylä","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Konstantinos","key":"manikaspau","last":"Manikas","locid":"749e6138-99be-4563-b6ef-a375c5f9ffa6","name":"Manikas, Konstantinos","orcid":"0000-0001-8531-898X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Mervi","key":"hämäläinenpau","last":"Hämäläinen","name":"Hämäläinen, Mervi","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Pasi","key":"tyrväinenpau","last":"Tyrväinen","name":"Tyrväinen, Pasi","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Slinger","key":"jansenpedh","last":"Jansen","name":"Jansen, Slinger","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Carina","key":"alvespedh","last":"Alves","name":"Alves, Carina","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"boschpedh","last":"Bosch","name":"Bosch, Jan","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"issn":["16130073"],"pages":"70-79","publisher":"CEUR-WS.org","series":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 8th Workshop on Software Ecosystems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019644533"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a568906d-4d32-44dd-9ecc-671a14fa6baf"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Designing, developing, and implementing software ecosystems : towards a step-wise guide","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-492248","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Software product evolution by means of improving their architecture, tools, or development methodologies are rather common in the lifetime of a software product. Especially if the product is in the domain of engineering where some of the basic calculation principles were established in some cases more than 50 years ago. However, a radical change of software products to evolve both in the software engineering as much as the organizational and business aspects in a disruptive manner are rather rare. In this paper, we report on the transformation of one of the market leader product series in water-related calculation and modeling from a traditional business-as-usual series of products to an evolutionary software ecosystem. We do so by relying on existing concepts on software ecosystem analysis to analyze the future ecosystem. We report and elaborate on the main focus points necessary for this transition. We argue for the generalization of our focus points to the transition from traditional business-as-usual software products to software ecosystems.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Manikas, Konstantinos"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382081"],"event":{"acronym":"ICSOB","title":"International Conference on Software Business"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Software ecosystems","ecosystem design","product modernization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evolving software products the design of a water related modeling software ecosystem","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83025404/Evolving_Software_Products.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382081","identifier":[{"id":"85034245018","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-36f67049-7904-433b-9842-1bcb6c8f45f3"],"keyword":["ecosystem design","product modernization","software ecosystems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A4CED05D084FE8C338533A8915DB359C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83025404/Evolving_Software_Products.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Konstantinos","key":"manikaspau","last":"Manikas","name":"Manikas, Konstantinos","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-69191-6_14","eisbn":["9783319691916"],"isbn":["9783319691909"],"issn":["18651348"],"pages":"192-198","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Business Information Processing","status":"p","subtitle":"ICSOB 2017","title":"International Conference of Software Business"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85034245018"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-36f67049-7904-433b-9842-1bcb6c8f45f3"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Evolving software products, the design of a water-related modeling software ecosystem.","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382081","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Compliance to regulations and regulatory approval are requirements for many medical device software systems. In this paper, we investigate the implications of medical device software regulations to the design of software systems. We do so by focusing on the American and European regulatory authorities and review the legal requirements for regulatory approval of medical devices. We define a simplified process for regulatory approval, consisting of five steps, and enhance this process by descriptions of how to decide whether a software system is a medical device and how to identify the class of the device. Moreover, we review software modularity in the implementation of software medical device and propose a set of preliminary principles for architectural design of software medical device based on a set of constrains identified from the reviewed regulations.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Hansen, Klaus Marius","Manikas, Konstantinos"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-446307"],"event":{"end":"2016-02-23","place":"Rome, it","start":"2016-02-21","title":"International Conference of Health Informatics","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on the impact of medical device regulations on software architecture","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-446307","identifier":[{"id":"84969247803","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-585e8a6c-8e59-49f8-9165-b475a8a0c5e1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E92467741AA7319D92B6A2409485052C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The HCC Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Klaus Marius","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d3f28440-9ea6-4c08-8622-11d418946f08","name":"Hansen, Klaus Marius","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Konstantinos","key":"manikaspau","last":"Manikas","locid":"749e6138-99be-4563-b6ef-a375c5f9ffa6","name":"Manikas, Konstantinos","orcid":"0000-0001-8531-898X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5220/0005776803890394","eisbn":["9789897581700"],"pages":"389-394","publisher":"SCITEPRESS Digital Library","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 9th International Joint Conference on Biomedical Engineering Systems and Technologies - Volume 5: HEALTHINF","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84969247803"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-585e8a6c-8e59-49f8-9165-b475a8a0c5e1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"On the impact of medical device regulations on software architecture","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-446307","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Software ecosystems - a topic with increasingly growing interest in academia and industry in the past decade - arguably revolutionized many aspects of industrial software engineering (business models, architectures, platforms, project executions, collaboration models, distribution of assets, to name a few). Software ecosystems enable the contribution of external actors with distinct center a common technology and the potential distribution of the actor contributions to an existing user set. Reference architectures have been proven successful and beneficial for software product lines and traditional software development within distinct domains. They arguably come with a set of benefits that severely counterweights the additional effort of design and implementation. But what is the role of reference architectures in an ecosystem setting? In this position paper, we argue for the use of reference architecture as a means of facilitating the operation of software ecosystems, supporting not only the technical aspects but also business and organizational. Thus, we propose that reference architectures can be used as a tool to facilitate software ecosystem orchestration and promote the ecosystem health. In this work, we identify a set of challenges and propose a research agenda for the further development of the field towards efficiently improving the existing means of ecosystem orchestration.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Knodel, Jens","Manikas, Konstantinos"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-466082"],"event":{"end":"2016-11-29","place":"København, dk","start":"2016-11-29","title":"4th International Workshop on Software Ecosystem Architectures","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Fraunhofer Institute for Experimental Software Engineering"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards reference architectures as an enabler for software ecosystems","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-466082","ids":["ku-795cec9a-5c50-4b4e-9057-afae6d533420"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-71BFAB447D80A16504622920FB40AE23"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"fraunhofer institute for experimental software engineering","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Fraunhofer Institute for Experimental Software Engineering","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The HCC Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"knodelpau","last":"Knodel","name":"Knodel, Jens","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Konstantinos","key":"manikaspau","last":"Manikas","locid":"749e6138-99be-4563-b6ef-a375c5f9ffa6","name":"Manikas, Konstantinos","orcid":"0000-0001-8531-898X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2993412.3003387","eisbn":["9781450347815"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proccedings of the 10th European Conference on Software Architecture Workshops"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-795cec9a-5c50-4b4e-9057-afae6d533420"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards reference architectures as an enabler for software ecosystems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-466082","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The field of software ecosystems is gradually transiting towards an established means of software development and distribution, counting numerous areas of applicability. However, research in software ecosystems, although the activity of over 10 years, is still characterized as premature with significant lack of software ecosystem specific theories that are solid, mature, generic, and detailed enough to be measurable and transferable. In this study, we intent to come closer to an evolution of the field by supporting the “localization” of research, i.e. the focus on specific types of software ecosystems. To do so, we investigate the literature of empirical, non open source ecosystem studies and intent to identify the various aspects and perspectives studied. In total, we review 56 empirical studies that investigate 55 software ecosystems. Our analysis confirms the assumption that proprietary software ecosystem studies lack deeper investigation of technical and collaborative aspects. Moreover, we identify an increased focus on organizational aspects and a rather limited focus on business. Furthermore, we identify common technology as the component investigated most in the ecosystems, both from the technical aspects, but also as means of applying orchestration. Finally, comparing the main areas with the overall ecosystem literature, we identify that empirical studies lack representation of health, motivation, actor activity, reusability, integration, and quality of ecosystems.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Manikas, Konstantinos"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-437550"],"event":{"acronym":"ICSOB","end":"2016-06-14","place":"Ljubljana, si","start":"2016-06-13","title":"7th International Conference on Software Business","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"supporting the evolution of research in software ecosystems reviewing the empirical literature","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-437550","identifier":[{"id":"84976646469","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-49db0713-6b26-416f-a8c7-20ccc3dc6f78"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-25158DE3706D44240E06E104E08B3D16"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The HCC Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Konstantinos","key":"manikaspau","last":"Manikas","locid":"749e6138-99be-4563-b6ef-a375c5f9ffa6","name":"Manikas, Konstantinos","orcid":"0000-0001-8531-898X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andrey","key":"maglyaspedh","last":"Maglyas","name":"Maglyas, Andrey","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anna-Lena","key":"lamprechtpedh","last":"Lamprecht","name":"Lamprecht, Anna-Lena","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-40515-5_5","eisbn":["9783319405155"],"isbn":["9783319405148"],"pages":"63-78","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","subtitle":"7th International Conference, ICSOB 2016, Ljubljana, Slovenia, June 13-14, 2016, Proceedings","title":"Software Business"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84976646469"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-49db0713-6b26-416f-a8c7-20ccc3dc6f78"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Supporting the evolution of research in software ecosystems : reviewing the empirical literature.","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-437550","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"‘Software ecosystems’ is argued to first appear as a concept more than 10 years ago and software ecosystem research started to take off in 2010. We conduct a systematic literature study, based on the most extensive literature review in the field up to date, with two primarily aims: (a) to provide an updated overview of the field and (b) to document evolution in the field. In total, we analyze 231 papers from 2007 until 2014 and provide an overview of the research in software ecosystems. Our analysis reveals a field that is rapidly growing both in volume and empirical focus while becoming more mature. We identify signs of field maturity from the increase in: (i) the number of journal articles, (ii) the empirical models within the last two years, and (iii) the number of ecosystem studied. However, we note that the field is far from mature and identify a set of as challenges preventing the field from evolving. We propose means for future research and the community to address them. Finally, our analysis shapes the view of the field having evolved outside the existing definitions of software ecosystems and thus propose the update of the definition of software ecosystems.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Manikas, Konstantinos"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-541468"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"revisiting software ecosystems research a longitudinal literature study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-541468","identifier":[{"id":"84960154891","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-f7f42e4a-6066-4bba-ad6a-171285e60d49"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F91D2238482B54BCDBB93DD70E0BB657"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The HCC Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Konstantinos","key":"manikaspau","last":"Manikas","locid":"749e6138-99be-4563-b6ef-a375c5f9ffa6","name":"Manikas, Konstantinos","orcid":"0000-0001-8531-898X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jss.2016.02.003","issn":["01641212","18731228"],"issn_org":["01641212"],"journal":"Journal of Systems and Software","pages":"84-103","status":"p","title":"Journal of Systems and Software","title_org":"The Journal of Systems and Software","volume":"117"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84960154891"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f7f42e4a-6066-4bba-ad6a-171285e60d49"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Revisiting software ecosystems research : a longitudinal literature study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-541468","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
